# To Bee or Not to Bee? (windurst 35): Zayhi-Bauhi, Raamimi, Kalupa-Tawalupa, Rutango-Botango (Windurst Walls; no
# default action, no container; the standards 299 / 296 / 298 / 297 are their scripts'). A level-75 WAR with 5 Pots of
# Honey. The Postman Always KO's Twice not completed: the four standards; a honey traded: nothing. Completed (GM), fame
# 49 (level 1): 299; 50: 64 (var 10, no quest); Kalupa-Tawalupa 66, Rutango-Botango 65; 64 again. Raamimi 67 with no
# free slot: ITEM_CANNOT_BE_OBTAINED, not begun; freed: begun, a honey. Accepted: Raamimi 68; Zayhi-Bauhi var 10: 64;
# two honeys: nothing; one: 69 (var 1); Kalupa-Tawalupa 72, Rutango-Botango 71; the trigger at var 1: 69 (var 1 again);
# then the honeys 70 (2), 73 (3), 74 (4) with a trigger at each, and 75: completed, fame 20, var 5, needToZone.
# Completed with needToZone: 78, 77, 76; Raamimi var 5: 80 with no free slot: ITEM_CANNOT_BE_OBTAINED (Mulsum); freed:
# var 0, 3 Mulsum, needToZone; then 79. needToZone with the quest available / accepted (GMs): 298 / 297. Rezoned: the
# four standards. Also: a honey while available: nothing; a honey and another item, or another item alone: nothing.
char zone=WindurstWalls pos=-88.0,-9.5,106.0 job=WAR lvl=75
fame Windurst 50
item PotOfHoney x5
login
trigger Zayhi-Bauhi                     # Postman not completed: his 299
finish
trade Zayhi-Bauhi PotOfHoney x1         # not accepted: nothing
